<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Eight-adult brain-coverage audit</title>
<style>body{font:16px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#203747;background:#f5f7f9;max-width:1140px;margin:auto;padding:40px 24px}h1{font-size:2.3rem;line-height:1.15;letter-spacing:-.035em}h2{margin-top:2.5rem}h3{margin-bottom:.5rem}p{max-width:95ch}.tag{font-size:13px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;color:#4e697c}.note{background:#fff2d8;border-left:4px solid #b67e22;padding:16px 20px}.table{overflow:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;background:white;font-size:13px;width:100%}th,td{padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8e1e7;text-align:left}th{vertical-align:bottom}img{max-width:100%;height:auto;background:white}dt{font-weight:600;margin-top:12px}dd{margin-left:0}a{color:#08688d}code{font-size:13px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}footer{font-size:13px;border-top:1px solid #ccd8e0;margin-top:30px;padding-top:15px}</style></head><body>
<div class="tag">fMRI Study Check · Separate descriptive supplement</div>
<h1>Does a computable matrix hide missing brain coverage?</h1>
<p>This audit retains the original eight adults, sub-pixar123 through sub-pixar130. It examines the existing tutorial source observations and independent archived SPM8 data. No primary connectivity result is recalculated, repaired, excluded or overwritten.</p>
<div class="note"><strong>Two evidence layers.</strong> The SPM8 mask is not the matching 2019 fMRIPrep mask. Tutorial temporal variation is a proxy affected by masking, interpolation and int8 quantization; it is not a brain mask or proof of neural signal. Do not pool or subtract these two percentages as a pipeline effect.</div>
<h2>Actual findings across the eight scans</h2>
<p>Completed audits: <strong>{{ summary|length }}/8</strong>. Acquisition or scan failures: <strong>{{ failures|length }}</strong>. All percentages below are descriptive; the 80% mask and 50% variation bins are project review conventions, not validated adequacy thresholds.</p>
<div class="table"><table id="participant-summary"><thead><tr><th>Participant</th><th>Primary status</th><th>Archived mask / cortical atlas</th><th>Regions with zero mask overlap</th><th>Regions below 80% mask overlap</th><th>Tutorial regions below 50% varying centers</th><th>Constant tutorial regional means</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for r in summary_rows %}<tr><td>{{ r.participant_id }}</td><td>{{ r.primary_status }}</td><td>{% if r.archived_mask_unknown_atlas_voxels == 0 %}{{ '%.1f'|format(r.archived_mask_cortical_atlas_fraction * 100) }}%{% else %}Unknown; see exported bounds{% endif %}</td><td>{{ r.archived_zero_mask_regions }}</td><td>{{ r.archived_regions_below_80pct }}</td><td>{{ r.tutorial_sparse_regions_below_50pct }}</td><td>{{ r.tutorial_constant_regional_means }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
<p><code>archived_mask_cortical_atlas_fraction</code> divides the number of full-atlas cortical voxel centers inside the SPM8 mask by all cortical atlas voxel centers. <code>archived_regions_below_80pct</code> counts parcels below the descriptive 0.8 mask-overlap bin. <code>tutorial_sparse_regions_below_50pct</code> counts parcels with fewer than half of their 4-mm voxel centers varying across the run. A valid regional average can be driven by a small surviving boundary fraction.</p>
<img src="{{ heatmap }}" alt="Two heatmaps, eight participants by 48 fixed atlas regions: independent mask overlap and tutorial temporal variation, separately labeled and scaled from zero to one">
<h2>Focused review: sub-pixar123 and sub-pixar124</h2>
{% for r in focus %}<h3>{{ r.participant_id }}</h3><p>Primary status remains <strong>{{ r.primary_status }}</strong>. Region 14 (Inferior Temporal Gyrus, anterior division): <strong>{{ r.tutorial_r14_grid_varying_voxels }}/{{ r.tutorial_r14_grid_voxels }}</strong> tutorial parcel voxel centers vary; <strong>{{ r.spm8_r14_atlas_mask_voxels }}/{{ r.spm8_r14_atlas_voxels }}</strong> full-atlas voxels lie inside the independent SPM8 mask. Region 37 (Temporal Fusiform Cortex, anterior division): <strong>{{ r.tutorial_r37_grid_varying_voxels }}/{{ r.tutorial_r37_grid_voxels }}</strong> tutorial centers vary; <strong>{{ r.spm8_r37_atlas_mask_voxels }}/{{ r.spm8_r37_atlas_voxels }}</strong> full-atlas voxels lie inside that mask.</p>{% endfor %}
<p>A <a href="{{ paper }}">published reanalysis</a> excluded both participants for poor brain coverage. That study used SPM12, a third preprocessing lineage. Its decisions provide context and are not imported into our primary results.</p>
{% for participant, figure in scan_figures %}<h3>{{ participant }}: saved source slices</h3><img src="{{ figure }}" alt="{{ participant }}: tutorial and independent SPM8 BOLD slices with region 14, region 37 and supplied SPM8 mask overlays">{% endfor %}
<h2>Methods, checks and interpretation</h2><dl>{% for key,value in settings.items() %}<dt>{{ key }}</dt><dd>{{ value }}</dd>{% endfor %}</dl>
<p>Identifiers and participant/role joins, filenames, source SHA-256 and published S3 MD5/ETag, image/mask dimensions and affine, binary mask values, full BOLD readability/finite observations, frame counts, original indices, atlas identities and explicit denominators are checked. Direct uncleaned regional means agree with saved primary raw series within the recorded numerical tolerance. Per-scan error values are in participant_summary.csv. No signal cleaning or censoring is performed in this supplement.</p>
<p>{{ issues_count }} region-level review flags are exported with observed evidence, file/region location, rule, possible explanations and recommended action. Flags do not automatically invalidate or approve a primary scan. Review the 48-region CSV for every scan, including scans with no exact constant regional averages.</p>
<h2>Unavailable evidence and limitations</h2><p>The exact 2019 fMRIPrep parent BOLD, brain masks and preprocessing HTML QA are absent from the materials used here. MRIQC 0.9.6 supplies native acquisition QA, not that missing preprocessing report. The SPM8 2-mm images are upsampled normalized data after 5-mm smoothing, not native 2-mm acquisitions. Native acquired-slab illustrations use scanner header coordinates only; no new registration or precise native-to-MNI parcel coverage is inferred. Masking, acquisition coverage, registration, atlas placement and quantization cannot be assigned separate causal contributions from these assets.</p>
{% for r in summary_rows %}{% if r.spm8_mask_nonfinite_voxels > 0 %}<p><strong>{{ r.participant_id }} mask missingness:</strong> the original archived mask has {{ r.spm8_mask_nonfinite_voxels }} NaN voxels. {{ r.archived_mask_unknown_atlas_voxels }} full-atlas cortical locations overlap these unknown values. Original voxel/world coordinates are exported in the participant's <code>mask_missing_locations.csv</code>. Undefined source values are preserved; a parcel fraction is unavailable, with lower/upper bounds exported, if unknown values overlap that parcel.</p>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{% if failures %}<h3>Specific failures</h3><pre>{{ failures|tojson(indent=2) }}</pre>{% endif %}
<h2>Next steps</h2><p>Inspect the spatial evidence with the investigator, obtain matching fMRIPrep files and registration QA, and prespecify a coverage policy before any separately versioned reanalysis. Numerical completeness and changed correlation matrices do not establish biological validity. The maintainer request remains an unsent draft.</p>
<h2>Attribution and reproduction</h2><p>Original study: Richardson et al. (2018), ds000228 R1.0.0. <a href="https://s3.amazonaws.com/openneuro/ds000228/ds000228_R1.0.0/uncompressed/derivatives/README">Archive methods</a>: SPM8/MATLAB despite the historical “fmriprep” folder name. <a href="https://osf.io/wjtyq/">Tutorial methods</a>: fMRIPrep 1.3.0.post2 followed by masking, 4-mm resampling and int8 distribution. Harvard–Oxford atlas provenance and dependency versions are recorded in provenance.json; complete source URLs, hashes and archive timestamps are in download_manifest.json.</p>
<pre><code>uv run python investigations/eight-adult-coverage/acquire.py
uv run python investigations/eight-adult-coverage/audit.py
uv run python investigations/eight-adult-coverage/audit.py --verify-only</code></pre>
<p>Content-based per-scan caches are held only in this supplement. Failed or missing assets remain explicit; completed work is preserved. The primary one- and eight-participant HTML reports and result bundles remain unchanged.</p>
<footer>Generated {{ generated_at }} · Protected files unchanged: {{ preservation.unchanged }} ({{ preservation.protected_file_count }} files). Self-contained report; observations are real public data.</footer>
</body></html>
